  "worked_solution": "We multiply each term inside the parentheses by the term outside the parentheses, simplify using the rules of exponents, and then we add the results together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x({x}^{2}y+2) & = \\\\ 3x({x}^{2}y)+3x(2) & = \\\\ 3\\cdot {x}^{2+1}y+6x & = \\\\ 3{x}^{3}y+6x\\end{aligned}\n$$",
